    "summary": "High‑energy Fall ’72 with soaring Bird Song and stellar Playing in the Band",
    "blurb": "The October 2, 1972 Springfield show crackles with high‑energy grooves and several standout jams – notably Bird Song, a marathon Playing In The Band, and a fiery Truckin' > Nobody's Fault > Feelin' Groovy sequence. Jerry’s soaring tone and Phil’s driving bass keep the band locked in, while Keith adds vivid color on the transitions. An excellent soundboard capture makes this a must‑listen for Fall ’72 fans.",
    "review": "The Dead bring their A‑game to Springfield Civic Center on October 2, 1972, delivering a setlist that bursts with vitality from start to finish. The first set rolls tight, highlighted by a smoking Bird Song where Jerry’s fat, soaring tone rides over Phil’s powerful bass and Keith’s forward‑in‑the‑mix keys. A standout Playing In The Band showcases inventive noodling and an extended water‑wavy solo that keeps the crowd riveted. The second set deepens the journey: a seamless China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segue, a heartfelt Stella Blue, and a legendary Truckin' > Nobody's Fault But Mine Jam > Feelin' Groovy stretch where Bill’s “sick” drumming drives the band into exhilarating territory. Though the later portion dips slightly with The Promised Land and He's Gone, the overall flow remains solid, capped off by a jubilant encore of Uncle John’s Band and Johnny B. Goode. The Miller soundboard capture (gd1972-10-02.sbd.gans.miller.112864.flac16) offers crystal‑clear guitars and keys, making this performance one of the most rewarding Fall ’72 documents available.",
